    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="0528" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg524"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/6593: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-27T15:00:00+08:00">February 27, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 27—9:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>130. My 95, February 8, 2 p.m.<anchor n="81" xml:id="d533-f1"/> I learned from
                    source near Soong<anchor n="82" xml:id="d533-f2"/> that C. T. Wang is being
                    recalled for apparently misinforming Government about prospects for loan in the
                    United States which Kung<anchor n="83" xml:id="d533-f3"/> hoped to apply to
                    purchase of planes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d533-f1" n="81" xml:id="d533-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d533-f2" n="82" xml:id="d533-f2-content">
                <p>T. V. Soong, chairman of the Board of Directors, Bank of China, and formerly
                    Chinese Minister of Finance.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d533-f3" n="83" xml:id="d533-f3-content">
                <p>H. H. Kung, President of the Chinese Executive Yuan (Premier) and Minister of
                    Finance.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
